      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for saying that but i really hate hospitals. i've had migraines for years and sometimes they get so bad i can barely walk or talk right. my doctor once said it was basically just a neurological overload. could it just be that? like, is there any way to tell if it's just a really bad migraine vs something else without having to pay for a massive ER bill? maybe some extra ibuprofen or something could help it pass?",
